        "original_id": "86f68873-8ada-533a-a603-88df2533bb11",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania; Washington Township; downtown Pittsburgh\n- Roads: Pennsylvania Route 380; Pennsylvania Route 780; Interstate 579; PA 380\n- Landmarks: PPG Paints Arena\n- People: Kathleen George\n- Organizations: Pittsburgh Penguins; National Hockey League; Pittsburgh Power; Arena Football League\n\nFacts:\n- Kathleen George was born on July 7, 1943.\n- Kathleen George is an American professor and writer best known for a series of crime novels set in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.\n- PPG Paints Arena is a multi-purpose indoor arena in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.\n- PPG Paints Arena serves as the home of the Pittsburgh Penguins of the National Hockey League.\n- PPG Paints Arena was the home of the Pittsburgh Power of the Arena Football League from 2011 to 2014.\n- Pennsylvania Route 380 is officially designated SR 400 because Interstate 380 exists elsewhere in Pennsylvania.\n- Pennsylvania Route 380 is also known as the J.F. Bonetto Memorial Highway and, within Pittsburgh, as Bigelow Boulevard, Baum Boulevard, and Frankstown Road.\n- Pennsylvania Route 380 is a 32.80-mile state highway in western Pennsylvania.\n- The western terminus of Pennsylvania Route 380 is at Interstate 579 in downtown Pittsburgh near PPG Paints Arena.\n- The eastern terminus of Pennsylvania Route 780 is at PA 380 in Washington Township.",
